---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Row from '../components/Row.astro';
import { outsideOfWork } from '../data/resume';
---

<Base
  title="About — Pranav Gillella"
  description="Carrollton, Texas to UIUC. Why I'm studying finance and computer science together, and what I'm building toward."
>
  <Row>
    <h1>About</h1>
  </Row>

  <Row class="prose">
    <p>
      I grew up in Carrollton, Texas, and I'm a freshman at the University of
      Illinois — finance in Gies, computer science minor in Grainger.
    </p>
    <p>
      Markets came first. In 2023 I won the Stock Market Game and was a national
      finalist in InvestWrite, and what stuck was not the winning. It was that a
      written argument about a company could be checked against what actually
      happened afterward. Code came second, through AP Computer Science, and it
      took me a while to notice the two were the same instinct: make the claim,
      then find out whether you were right.
    </p>
    <p>
      That's why I'm doing both rather than picking one. Finance without
      programming means taking someone else's numbers on faith. Programming
      without finance means building tools with no view about what's worth
      measuring.
    </p>
    <p>
      I run Quant Labs LLC, which is two products I built and operate alone.
      EarlyDMV rebooks Texas DPS driver license appointments into earlier slots.
      Protestly files property tax protests for Denton County homeowners and
      argues them at the appraisal review board. Both are live, both have paying
      customers, and both are hosted on hardware I manage myself.
    </p>
    <p>
      What I'm working toward is quant research or trading. The <a
        href="/projects/ma-crossover-backtest">backtester</a
      > is where that starts — I wrote the metrics from scratch specifically so I'd
      understand what they hide.
    </p>
  </Row>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <Row class="row--head">
    <h2>Outside of work</h2>
    <ul class="plain">
      {outsideOfWork.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </Row>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <Row>
    <p>
      More detail on <a href="/experience">experience and skills</a>, or the <a
        href="/resume">résumé</a
      >.
    </p>
  </Row>
</Base>

<style>
  .plain {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .plain li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
